The general term in the expansion of \({\left(2^{1/3} + \frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{n}\) is given by:
T_{r+1} = {^{n}C_{r}} {\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-r} {\left(\frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{r}

### Step 1: Find the 15th term from the beginning (T_15)

For the \(15^{th}\) term from the beginning, we set \(r = 14\):
T_{15} = {^{n}C_{14}} {\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-14} {\left(\frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{14}

### Step 2: Find the 15th term from the end (T'_15)

The \(15^{th}\) term from the end is the \((n - 15 + 1)^{th}\) term from the beginning, which is the \((n - 14)^{th}\) term from the beginning. So, we set \(r = n - 14\):
T'_{15} = T_{(n-14)+1} = {^{n}C_{n-14}} {\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-(n-14)} {\left(\frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{n-14}
Simplifying this, we get:
T'_{15} = {^{n}C_{n-14}} {\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{14} {\left(\frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{n-14}

### Step 3: Use the given ratio to find n

We are given that the ratio of the \(15^{th}\) term from the beginning to the \(15^{th}\) term from the end is \(\frac{1}{6}\):
\frac{T_{15}}{T'_{15}} = \frac{{^{n}C_{14}} {\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-14} {\left(\frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{14}}{{^{n}C_{n-14}} {\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{14} {\left(\frac{1}{3^{1/3}}\right)}^{n-14}} = \frac{1}{6}
Since \(^{n}C_{r} = {^{n}C_{n-r}}\), we have \(^{n}C_{14} = {^{n}C_{n-14}}\). These terms cancel out.
\frac{{\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-14} {\left(3^{-1/3}\right)}^{14}}{{\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{14} {\left(3^{-1/3}\right)}^{n-14}} = \frac{1}{6}
Combine the terms with the same base:
{\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-14-14} {\left(3^{-1/3}\right)}^{14-(n-14)} = \frac{1}{6}
{\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-28} {\left(3^{-1/3}\right)}^{28-n} = \frac{1}{6}
{\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-28} {\left(3^{1/3}\right)}^{-(28-n)} = \frac{1}{6}
{\left(2^{1/3}\right)}^{n-28} {\left(3^{1/3}\right)}^{n-28} = \frac{1}{6}
{\left(2 \cdot 3\right)}^{(n-28)/3} = 6^{-1}
6^{(n-28)/3} = 6^{-1}
Equating the exponents:
\frac{n-28}{3} = -1
n-28 = -3
n = 25

### Step 4: Calculate the value of \(^{n}C_{3}\)

Now, substitute \(n = 25\) into \(^{n}C_{3}\):
{^{25}C_{3}} = \frac{25 \times 24 \times 23}{3 \times 2 \times 1}
{^{25}C_{3}} = 25 \times 4 \times 23
{^{25}C_{3}} = 100 \times 23
{^{25}C_{3}} = 2300

