The general term in the binomial expansion of \((2+x)^9\) is given by \(T_{r+1} = {}^{9}C_{r} 2^{9-r} x^r\). The coefficient of \(x^r\) is \({}^{9}C_{r} 2^{9-r}\).
We need to find the mean of the coefficients of \(x, x^2, ..., x^7\), which corresponds to \(r = 1, 2, ..., 7\). There are 7 coefficients in total.
The coefficients are:
\text{Coefficient of } x: {}^{9}C_{1} 2^{8}
\text{Coefficient of } x^2: {}^{9}C_{2} 2^{7}
and so on, up to
\text{Coefficient of } x^7: {}^{9}C_{7} 2^{2}
The mean is the sum of these coefficients divided by 7:
\text{Mean} = \frac{{}^{9}C_{1} 2^{8} + {}^{9}C_{2} 2^{7} + \dots + {}^{9}C_{7} 2^{2}}{7}
We know the sum of all coefficients in the expansion is \(\sum_{r=0}^{9} {}^{9}C_{r} 2^{9-r} = (2+1)^9 = 3^9\). The sum in the numerator can be found by subtracting the coefficients for \(r=0, 8, 9\) from the total sum.
\text{Sum} = (\sum_{r=0}^{9} {}^{9}C_{r} 2^{9-r}) - ({}^{9}C_{0} 2^{9} + {}^{9}C_{8} 2^{1} + {}^{9}C_{9} 2^{0})
\text{Mean} = \frac{(2+1)^{9} - ({}^{9}C_{0} 2^{9} + {}^{9}C_{8} 2^{1} + {}^{9}C_{9})}{7}
= \frac{3^{9} - (1 \cdot 2^{9} + 9 \cdot 2 + 1)}{7}
= \frac{19683 - 512 - 18 - 1}{7}
= \frac{19152}{7}
= 2736

For the expansion of \((\alpha x^{3} + \frac{1}{\beta x})^{11}\), the general term is:
T_{r+1} = {}^{11}C_{r} (\alpha x^{3})^{11-r} \left(\frac{1}{\beta x}\right)^{r}
= {}^{11}C_{r} \alpha^{11-r} \beta^{-r} x^{3(11-r)-r} = {}^{11}C_{r} \alpha^{11-r} \beta^{-r} x^{33-4r}
To find the coefficient of \(x^{9}\), we set the power of \(x\) to 9:
